<section id="A1.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.5.1 </span>Importance of Joint Retrieval and Fine-tuning</h4>

<figure id="A1.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 8</span>: </span><span id="A1.T8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Ablation for fine-tuning. Applying TabPFN-<math id="A1.T8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>NN on a fine-tuned model degrades the overall performance. On the other hand, performing local calibration by jointly retrieving and fine-tuning improve performance drastically. </span></figcaption>
